## ARTICLE 7. CONDITIONS TO CLOSING

**7.1 Conditions to Obligations of Each Party.** The obligations of each party to consummate the Closing are subject to the satisfaction, at or before the Closing, of the following conditions:

(a) any applicable waiting period under the HSR Act shall have expired or been terminated; and

(b) no Governmental Authority shall have enacted or issued any Law or order that is in effect and makes the transactions contemplated by this Agreement illegal or otherwise restrains or prohibits their consummation.

**7.2 Conditions to Obligations of Buyer.** The obligations of Buyer to consummate the Closing are subject to the satisfaction or waiver by Buyer, at or before the Closing, of the following additional conditions:

(a) the Fundamental Representations shall be true and correct in all respects, and all other representations and warranties of Seller in Article 4 shall be true and correct in all material respects (or, for representations qualified by materiality or Material Adverse Effect, in all respects), in each case as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date;

(b) Seller shall have performed and complied in all material respects with all covenants and agreements required by this Agreement to be performed or complied with by it before or at the Closing;

(c) Seller shall have obtained the OEM Supply Consent and made the regulatory filings set forth in Section 4.5 of the Disclosure Schedule, in each case in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to Buyer;

(d) the Key Employee Agreement shall be in full force and effect;

(e) Buyer shall have received a certificate, dated the Closing Date and signed by a duly authorized officer of Seller, certifying that the conditions in Sections 7.2(a), 7.2(b) and 7.2(f) have been satisfied;

(f) since the date of this Agreement, there shall not have occurred any Material Adverse Effect; and

(g) Seller shall have delivered each of the items set forth in Section 3.2.

**7.3 Conditions to Obligations of Seller.** The obligations of Seller to consummate the Closing are subject to the satisfaction or waiver by Seller, at or before the Closing, of the following additional conditions:

(a) the representations and warranties of Buyer in Article 5 shall be true and correct in all material respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date;

(b) Buyer shall have performed and complied in all material respects with all covenants and agreements required by this Agreement to be performed or complied with by it before or at the Closing; and

(c) Seller shall have received a certificate, dated the Closing Date and signed by a duly authorized officer of Buyer, certifying that the conditions in Sections 7.3(a) and 7.3(b) have been satisfied, and Buyer shall have delivered each of the items set forth in Section 3.3.

## ARTICLE 8. TERMINATION

**8.1 Termination.** This Agreement may be terminated at any time before the Closing:

(a) by mutual written consent of Buyer and Seller;

(b) by either party, by written notice to the other, if the Closing has not occurred on or before [●], 2027 (the "**Outside Date**"), provided that this right is not available to a party whose breach of this Agreement caused the failure of the Closing to occur by that date;

(c) by Buyer, by written notice to Seller, if Seller has breached any representation, warranty or covenant such that a condition in Section 7.2(a) or 7.2(b) would not be satisfied, and the breach is not cured within 30 days after written notice of it;

(d) by Seller, by written notice to Buyer, if Buyer has breached any representation, warranty or covenant such that a condition in Section 7.3(a) or 7.3(b) would not be satisfied, and the breach is not cured within 30 days after written notice of it; or

(e) by either party if any final and non-appealable order of a Governmental Authority permanently restrains or prohibits the transactions contemplated by this Agreement.

**8.2 Effect of Termination.** If this Agreement is terminated under Section 8.1, it shall become void and of no further effect without liability of any party, except that (a) this Section 8.2 and Article 11 survive termination, and (b) nothing in this Section 8.2 relieves any party from liability for any willful breach of this Agreement occurring before termination.

## ARTICLE 9. SURVIVAL

**9.1 Survival.** The representations and warranties in this Agreement survive the Closing until the date that is 18 months after the Closing Date, except that (a) the Fundamental Representations survive until the date that is six years after the Closing Date, and (b) the representations in Section 4.14 survive until 60 days after expiration of the applicable statute of limitations. The covenants and agreements in this Agreement survive the Closing in accordance with their terms. Any claim asserted in writing with reasonable specificity before expiration of the applicable survival period survives until finally resolved.

